  "behavioral_corrections": [
    "Replace caller-selected owner epochs with generations minted from the durable row under a SQLite write transaction.",
    "Reject acquisition while a held generation is live, reject clock regression and signed-SQLite overflow, and compare-and-replace on the exact prior generation.",
    "Propagate the exact session/daemon/worker/lock-id/generation capability through checkpoint mutation orchestration.",
    "Re-read and authorize the durable owner row inside the same recipient write transaction as each guarded mutation.",
    "Fence release as an exact transition rather than allowing descriptive lock observations to retire a generation.",
    "Hold an immediate SQLite write reservation across staged-byte publication and stale-artifact removal so a compliant takeover cannot interleave mid-effect.",
    "Move acquisition and release row interpretation out of sync_domain.cpp into a focused runtime owner, preserving the monolith budget rather than weakening it."
  ],
